at he crafted the crest  of the rat for the Rat King to give to  humans for humans could activate the  traps to defend the Burrow and who knows  maybe eventually trust in humans could  be slowly repaired my servant well met  indeed would seem some sunlight poisoned  creatures are worthy of great honor the  host permitted me to dream one day rats  and humans may yet live and die together  in peace so where do we find furrows  well here's a perfect example of how the  story branches out let's look at this  skeleton here it's placed really honor  airily and it almost makes me think that  it could be pharaohs or perhaps it's a  man named Havel who is referred to in  the associated bonfire warp zone for  this area if it's even significant at  all then I personally lean towards it  being hvar since the bonfire refers to  him having a resting place here and you  can just see this skeleton from below as  you traverse this zone another reason I  like to think it might be hovel is  because I can imagine Ferris still being  further below speaking of names they  call this place the grave of saints and  I'd say that the red phantom of one  Saint can be found further down in new  game+ you are attacked by the red  phantom of a cleric who wears the exact  same armor as the fire keeper in Dark  Souls 1 down to the very blood-stained  skirt that she wears somebody told me  that de grève of a saint lies below here  not built by the king no no it did back  to our time long before him so in Dark  Souls 1 anestachio was a fire keeper  with the dingy set and both said  descriptions tell us that the smoke and  the ashes of the bonfires have darkened  them over the years Anastasia's skirt  was blood-stained  and I always took this to mean that law  Trek did this when he killed her but I  could be wrong on that and maybe the  blood stain has to do with the fact that  she was disfigured in some way for we  know that she had her tongue cut out so  that she couldn't speak up against the  Lord's either way what appears to be  this  same character is here in the grave of  saints a place that existed way before  the current king of this land I don't  know much about red fountains and Dark  Souls lore in Demon Souls they had an  explanation you know when you died in  spirit form you came back as a hostile  red phantom but in the Dark Souls  universe I guess the only way to see  them is as hostile spirits or something  like that moving on from that fairly  indigestible piece of law let's talk  about the gutter in general I love this  area  so it's frequently referred to as the  place where everything unwanted or  tossed away ends up and honestly this  was my favorite area on my first  playthrough it's the first and I reckon  the only area to make use of the  lighting system and just coming down  here with a torch to help you see and  seeing the massive trash flowing down  towards the bottom it really conveyed  this powerful theme of things being  thrown away and things that would never  see the surface again and this is really  enforced by this one moment where you  drop through a roof into what could  actually be called a living area you see  rugs pots furniture it's all these  things that man would put around to make  it more homely and so all of a sudden  this family of hollows has you crashed  down into this home that they'd made for  themselves and it's this tiny brief  glimpse of humanity in a place that's  notoriously devoid of it and you crash  through and the hollows defend their  home and you cut them all down without a  second thought  because this is dark souls and you kill  whatever's in front of you and I had  just been startled as I crushed through  here and I didn't take in my  surroundings I just wanted to survive I  killed everything that came at me and  then in the aftermath I thought and  maybe you did too that the little homely  Touches of this area were significant  because sometimes we're not really the  good guy in this game you know and this  brief experience started to form the  foundations of what I think about the  gutter in general I like to think that  all the humans down here you know  however they ended up here whether there  were just hollowed corpse thrown down  here so they wouldn't be seen again I  just think that maybe they were trying  to build their way out with this wooden  structure or something like that and  this thought even though it's not  confirmed you know  it's just a brief thought that I had it  really gave more weight to this area for  me another being in the gutter is the  giant ant queen the guide suggests that  it began its life in lord aldia z'  laboratory and it eventually lived its  usefulness it lays here passive dosel  away from its natural habitat and  discarded like everything else in the  gutter if you got poisoned by those  little poisonous ticks that guard it  then maybe you noticed that it actually  cures poison and I really appreciate  that they made it passive and looking  away from you like that you know you're  initially startled you don't expect to  see it but then you really start to feel  a little bit of pity for this misplaced  creature and then there are these  statues put around the place Gilligan  reckons that there might be the remnants  of some pagan cult but there is no real  explanation for them one theory I read  online is that they represent the  Emerald Herald they look a fair bit like  ER with the hood and the way they're  posed the fact that there's hundreds of  them could make you think that they were  created to honor someone but honestly in  my opinion I think they might have been  created as more of an obsession than to  honor someone there's one of them being  hung within the gutter which is this  really grim image and there's another  thing I came up with you also have to  consider that they spit poison which  could be fairly metaphorical for  spitting lies you know vitriol if it  does represent the herald then perhaps  someone created them out of spite we  know one character at least who thinks  that the words of the Emerald Herald are  a bunch of nonsense they say that she is  the last fire keeper but they say a lot  of things that she's a gentle shepherd  lighting the way for you cursed fools  nonsense and finally we get to the  rotten who we disturb as he attempts to  fix one of the statues is he responsible  for them is this his obsession is this  where he gets his happiness from maybe  he's upset because we're the ones going  through cutting all their heads off in  new game+ you realize that he has the  soul of the old dead one which was neato  in Dark Souls 1 just like neato he  aggravates things to him to create a  hole but the  cotton is a bit more intriguing to me  when you wait outside his fog gate you  can actually hear him crying from  outside and I assume that this was all  the tortured souls that were fused to  him when you cut off his left hand he  drops a Pharaoh's lock stone which has  led a lot of people to believe that he  might be pharaohs known for creating  traps and may be responsible for  creating the statues but ultimately what  do you think you make your own story in  the gutter and that's kind of what I  wanted to get out with this video it's a  good example of how the story can branch  and most of the ideas that you read in  the comment section I reckon they'll be  pretty valid but if you're looking for  more solid interpretations of the law  then check out my video I did recently  on the overall story of Dark Souls 2 the  story of the king and the queen is my  favorite in a souls game so far and I  think that you'll understand why if you  watch that video if you're looking for  more videos like these though then  you're going to be in luck because I  think the next few weeks I'm going to  devote to exploring the rest of  drangleic through story mode and through  10 things you missed so that we can get  a good understanding of the world before  we start going a b